# Every path is the app's, not a file on disk.
#
# This is a single-page app: the router owns /home, /settings, /destination/... —
# none of which exist as files. Without this a host looks for them, fails, and
# serves a 404 instead of the app, so a shared link or a refresh breaks.
#
# 200 rather than 301: the browser keeps the URL it asked for, which is what lets
# the router read it. Netlify and Cloudflare Pages both read this file; hosts that
# do not simply ignore it.
/*    /index.html   200
